# Task 150-009 Execution Plan: Auditor Stale Alert Race Condition Fix

## Analysis
Sprint 149 already implemented the core fix in `src/monitor/auditor.ts` (lines 293-316):
- Task JSON is read to check lifecycle state before generating stale alerts
- PENDING/CLAIMED/DRAFT/PAUSED tasks skip stale alerts entirely
- DONE/NO_GO tasks get WARNING (downgraded from CRITICAL)
- Only EXECUTING/TESTING/DOCUMENTING tasks trigger genuine CRITICAL stale alerts

`src/core/heartbeat-types.ts` exports `ACTIVE_EXECUTION_STATUSES`, `COMPLETED_STATUSES`, `PRE_EXECUTION_STATUSES` sets — but auditor.ts was using inline `new Set()` instead.

Tests in `tests/orchestra/auditor-stale-race.test.ts` cover all 5 required scenarios.

## Changes Made (Sprint 150 DRY Improvement)
1. Import `ACTIVE_EXECUTION_STATUSES` and `COMPLETED_STATUSES` from `heartbeat-types.ts`
2. Replace inline `EXECUTING_STATES` set with shared `ACTIVE_EXECUTION_STATUSES`
3. Replace inline `task.status === TaskStatus.DONE || task.status === TaskStatus.NO_GO` with `COMPLETED_STATUSES.has(task.status)`

## Verification
- tsc --noEmit: 0 errors
- vitest: 5/5 tests passing
